CK02 -- the replacement coupling for the clock sector

====================================================================================================
1. g~ = g + B n n: the photon cone (on g~) vs the graviton cone (on g), in the clock's rest frame
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] 1a photons on g~ move at sqrt(1 - B) relative to gravitons on g (whose cone is |k0| = |k1|): the cones differ by B/2 at first order, exactly as the record's gw170817_check found
           (v_photon^2 = 1 - B, split = -B/2)
  [PASS] 1b moving the disformal term to the gravitational sector only flips the sign of the split (photons faster by B/2): the difference is a property of the PAIR of metrics, so no assignment of the term removes it -- one metric for every species is the only cure
           (other assignment: v_photon - v_graviton = B/2)

====================================================================================================
2. one metric: the photon and graviton cones coincide for every potential, so the GW170817 delay is identically zero
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] 2a on one metric the photon's coordinate speed sqrt((1 - 2U)/(1 + 2V)) is the graviton's too: the arrival difference is 0 for any U, V (including the phantom's log potential): GW170817 satisfied by structure, not by a number
           (v^2 = (1 - 2*U)/(2*V + 1) for both roots)

